# BioBand Audio Rules

## Library
- Use `expo-audio` — never `expo-av`
- Preload with `preload()` when available (SDK 55+); on SDK 54 use `createAudioPlayer()` pool at init
- Use `useAudioPlayer()` or a shared player pool for low-latency playback

## Sample Playback
```typescript
// Preload at module scope for instant playback
import { preload, useAudioPlayer } from 'expo-audio';

preload(require('../assets/samples/C4.wav'));

// In component: player.play() on touch
```

## Recording (Phase 4+)
- Event-based recording: `{ note, timestamp, velocity }[]`
- Do NOT use microphone capture for instrument tracks
- Store recordings locally via AsyncStorage or expo-file-system

## Performance
- Prefer local bundled WAV samples over remote URLs
- Limit simultaneous active players; reuse where possible
- Test latency on real Android device via Expo Go
